        "original_id": "f037519e-3031-5c99-a9cb-5729344d9d22",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Filipendula, Aloinopsis, Aruncus, Aruncus dioicus\n- Taxonomy: genera, species, Rosaceae, type species\n- Places: South Africa, Northern Hemisphere\n\nFacts:\n- Filipendula is a genus of 12 species of perennial herbaceous flowering plants in the family Rosaceae.\n- Filipendula is native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere.\n- Aloinopsis is a genus of ice plants from South Africa.\n- Aruncus is closely related to the genera Filipendula and Spiraea.\n- Aruncus is native to mountainous damp woodland in temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere.\n- Aruncus dioicus is a flowering herbaceous perennial plant in the family Rosaceae.\n- Aruncus dioicus is known as goat's beard, buck's-beard, or bride's feathers.\n- Aruncus dioicus is the type species of the genus Aruncus.",
